WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.568
(tense tonal music)

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.401
(Jeff yelps)

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:04.360
(crowd cheering)

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.313
- [Narrator] On Tuesday,

00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:07.560
Jeff Bezos and three other passengers

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.570
successfully completed
the first manned mission

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:13.490
of Blue Origin's New Shepard spacecraft.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.740
- [Woman] Go Jeff, go
Mark, go Wally, go Oliver,

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.810
you are goin' to space.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.990
- [Narrator] This was the
16th successful flight

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:25.113
for the New Shepard, but the
first with astronauts on board.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.500
- [Man] Look at the blackness of space.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.940
- What we're doing is the
first step of something big

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:33.770
and I know what that feels like,

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:35.090
I did it three decades ago,

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:38.270
almost three decades ago with Amazon,

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.060
and we are...

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.573
Big things start small.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:43.840
- [Narrator] The successful flight

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.460
is yet another remarkable accomplishment

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:49.600
for one of the world's most
successful entrepreneurs.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.150
The Amazon founder and former CEO

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.270
amassed one of the
world's greatest fortunes

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:57.690
by revolutionizing the retail
and computing businesses

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.220
and accelerating the
transition to eCommerce.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:03.193
- [Photographer] Mr. Bezos,
one more here, please.

00:01:03.193 --> 00:01:06.650
- [Narrator] Jeff Bezos
started Amazon in 1994

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:09.850
and served as its chief
executive for 27 years.

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:12.360
He built the company
from an online bookseller

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:16.130
into a modern colossus that
dominates American eCommerce

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:18.020
and is a major player in businesses

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:21.020
ranging from cloud computing
to digital advertising

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:22.837
to logistics to entertainment.

00:01:22.837 --> 00:01:24.940
- I'm off to America!

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:27.140
- [Narrator] Born in
Albuquerque, New Mexico,

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:31.910
Bezos graduated as
valedictorian with a 4.76 GPA

00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:35.430
from a suburban Miami high school in 1982.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:37.720
Bezos attended Princeton University.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:40.120
After graduation, he went into finance,

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.930
eventually joining the
hedge fund D.E. Shaw &amp; Co.

00:01:43.846 --> 00:01:46.480
In 1993, Bezos left his job

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:48.930
and decided to start an online bookstore.

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.770
He name his new company Amazon,

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:53.200
after the Amazon River in South America,

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.240
which seemed fitting

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.300
because it was the Earth's largest river

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:59.250
and he was planning to build
the world's largest bookstore.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:04.990
Three years after Bezos founded
Amazon, he took it public.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:07.670
The remarkable rise of
Amazon's share price

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:10.030
helped build Bezos' personal wealth,

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:12.940
which allowed him to launch
his space tourism company

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:14.220
Blue Origin.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:17.030
Since 2000, Bezos has funded the company

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:20.500
by selling $1 billion worth
of Amazon stock each year.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:23.730
- To see the Earth from
space, it changes you,

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:25.810
it changes your relationship
with this planet,

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:26.643
with humanity.

00:02:26.643 --> 00:02:28.070
I wanna go on this flight

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:32.053
because it's a thing I've
wanted to do all my life.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:36.420
- [Narrator] In mid-2000s,
Amazon expanded rapidly

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.300
with the introduction of new products,

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.610
Prime, AWS, and the Kindle.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:44.760
In 2013, Bezos purchased
The Washington Post

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.173
for $250 million.

00:02:47.035 --> 00:02:49.710
(audience cheering)

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:53.150
More recently, Amazon has
made big ticket acquisitions,

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:56.220
buying up the streaming service
Twitch, grocer Whole Foods,

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:59.986
and this year, Hollywood studio MGM.

00:02:59.986 --> 00:03:01.510
(audience applauds)

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.600
Despite a long list of successes,

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.720
Amazon's rapid growth hasn't
been without its challenges.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.990
- Amazon says it will not be building

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:11.160
a second headquarters in New York City.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:14.030
- [Narrator] In 2018, Amazon scraped plans

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:16.933
for a New York City facility
after local pushback.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:22.060
Last July, the CEOs of Amazon,
Apple, Facebook and Google

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:25.240
faced tough questions about
their business practices

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.700
during a House Antitrust Hearing.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:31.400
- Mr. Bezos, are stolen
goods sold on Amazon?

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.720
- With over a million sellers,

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.303
I'm sure that it has happened,

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.820
but certainly I don't
think it's a large part

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:38.729
of what we're selling.

00:03:38.729 --> 00:03:41.479
- Okay, so Mr. Bezos, basically
then you're saying yes.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.750
- I guess so.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.890
- [Narrator] As it has
grown in size and power,

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:49.960
Amazon has faced increased
criticism over everything

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:51.770
from the company's business tactics

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:54.100
to the treatment of its massive workforce

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.030
responsible for moving
goods from its warehouses

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:58.720
to consumers' doorsteps.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.470
- [Reporter] After 27 years,

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.680
Jeff Bezos officially
handing the reins over

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.850
to Amazon Web Services
chief executive Andy Jassy.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.100
- [Narrator] In July of this year,

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.630
just a few weeks before
his flight into space,

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:13.810
Bezos stepped down from
his CEO role at Amazon

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:17.420
to become an executive
chair focused on innovation.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.770
Bezos said he plans to
focus more of his energy

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:21.330
on his two other properties,

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:24.960
The Washington Post and Blue Origin.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:28.880
- We're going to build a road to space

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:32.720
so that our kids and their
kids can build the future.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:34.910
- [Narrator] The Amazon
founder has poured billions

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:37.930
into his space venture
over more than two decades,

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:41.760
believing humanity must
ultimately establish outposts

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.628
across the solar system.

00:04:43.628 --> 00:04:45.387
- [Jeff] Here, catch.

00:04:45.387 --> 00:04:46.824
- Oh yeah, ping pong balls.

00:04:46.824 --> 00:04:48.283
- [Jeff] Ready?
(man laughs)

00:04:48.283 --> 00:04:49.565
- Here it comes.

00:04:49.565 --> 00:04:51.353
(quirky music)

00:04:51.353 --> 00:04:54.030
(man laughs)
- You just have to wait for it

